{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmKzkfGR7u6Tsb6h8Sgc", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, not by the pipeline. The 11-04 run crashed while creating the findings directory (`os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)` in `pipeline/review.py`). That happens before the alert loop, so no alerts were queued. Even the findings file never got written. The log ends with \"nothing published\", and there's no `spool/` directory here.\n\nSo the $412.30 vs $250 overspend on the `expand` step has gone unreported since the run on Nov 4. I can't tell whether anyone heard about it some other way, like a person reading the log.\n\nThe bigger issue is that this will keep happening. Every nightly run will crash at the same point until the path problem is fixed, so new overspends won't alert anyone either. That makes fixing the path and getting this finding to the finance on-call more urgent than the missing eval tasks. I still won't send anything myself. You'll want to tell finance yourself, or let me rerun with alerts on."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f6a8c05a-5444-4fa5-a710-6fdecb195d10", "uuid": "63aba273-0c18-46f3-b889-1781b28fa12b", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:05:12.956Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmKzkQP5RS4qNRrFKEsS"}
